* MathFn2 component reference -- the "## Example" netlist verbatim.
* No title line -- see doc-verify/const/example.cir's own comment for why.
*
* H is the textbook 3-4-5 triangle (hypot(3,4) = 5). AW shows anglewrap: the atan2-style angle
* of the same pair, wrapped into [0, 2*pi) instead of (-pi, pi] -- atan2(4,3) = 0.9273... rad.
* See test_mathfn.py::test_example_fn2_hypot_and_anglewrap.
X kind=const value=3
Y kind=const value=4
H kind=hypot in1=X in2=Y
AW kind=anglewrap in1=X in2=Y
